# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Local tooling state
.origin/
tools/__pycache__/

# Session event streams are tracked; session working directories are not.
# The contents pattern is load-bearing: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so `sessions/*/` makes the negations dead and
# `finish --push` cannot commit a session record without -f (observed on
# git 2.25.1, 2026-10-11).
sessions/*/*
!sessions/*/events.jsonl
!sessions/*/commands.log
!sessions/*/README.md

# Experiment raw data is tracked; bulk re-fetchable inputs are not
EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/**
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/*.jsonl
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/*.tsv
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/*.csv
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/*.json
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/*.md
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/SOURCES.md
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/SOURCES.json
!EXPERIMENTS/*/raw/CORPUS.json

# Specific experiment bulk inputs
# E037's 154 real git repositories (1.2 GB): re-fetchable from GitHub
EXPERIMENTS/037-line-staging/repos/
# E065's CFPB bulk archive (5.5 GB expanded, 352 MB zipped) from
# files.consumerfinance.gov/ccdb/. The record is raw/SOURCES.md - url, sha256
# and bytes per file - plus the 10,000-row sample process_csv.py wrote
# (raw/cfpb_complaints.jsonl), which is tracked, by the same clause as sdists/.
EXPERIMENTS/065-cfpb-complaint-harvest/raw/complaints.csv
EXPERIMENTS/065-cfpb-complaint-harvest/raw/complaints.csv.zip
# E070's CFPB bulk archive (5.5 GB expanded, 352 MB zipped) from
# files.consumerfinance.gov/ccdb/. The record is raw/SOURCES.md - url, sha256
# and bytes per file - plus the 10,000-row sample process_csv.py wrote
# (raw/cfpb_complaints.jsonl), which is tracked, by the same clause as sdists/.
EXPERIMENTS/070-discourse-fresh-observation/raw/complaints.csv
EXPERIMENTS/070-discourse-fresh-observation/raw/complaints.csv.zip
# E072's corpus: 36 REAL bank exports belonging to identifiable people, 3.6 MB
# across 43 files, fetched from raw.githubusercontent.com. The record is
# raw/SOURCES.json - repo, path, url, bytes and sha256 per file, plus the column
# names, row count and date span finalize.py computed from them. `finalize.py`
# re-hashes every file on each run and refuses a corpus whose bytes do not match
# their record. This is the same clause as E070's CFPB bulk archive and it is
# the one that matters most here, because these files are other people's bank
# statements rather than a published dataset: they are read, hashed, counted and
# never copied into the repository. raw/CORPUS.json IS tracked, because it
# carries no descriptor strings -- only account ids, hashes, row counts and the
# reason each exclusion fired.
EXPERIMENTS/072-merchant-noise-raw/raw/accounts/
# E068's 25 shallow clones of arXiv papers' repositories (3.6 GB, including
# multi-hundred-MB model checkpoints) and its PyPI metadata cache (392
# packages). Both are re-fetchable inputs, not record: the record is
# repos/MANIFEST.json for the checkouts - owner, repo, origin url and commit
# sha per repository, written by repos_manifest.py, so `git clone --depth 1`
# at that sha reproduces them - and for the cache it is generation_results.json
# plus pin_compatibility.py, which reads only the cached metadata and re-derives
# every figure in E069's results.json from it. Tracking the bytes would make
# `doc lint` walk third-party source trees and 3.6 GB of binary weights.
EXPERIMENTS/068-arxiv-spec-generator/repos/
EXPERIMENTS/068-arxiv-spec-generator/cache/pypi/
# E069's per-repository raw install records are small, and ARE tracked: they
# are the observation every gate in results.json is computed from, and the
# README's numbers are checked against them.

# Vendor skills: tracked as source, not as generated
vendor/

# Generated indexes
docs/INDEX.md
sessions/INDEX.md
tasks/INDEX.md

